  "scopeNotes": [
    "W3A preparation only; no runtime evidence is produced by this JSON.",
    "Serve only frozen product /home/b/.cache/gs-safety-ci.u7pR52 with matching production BUILD_ID and approved candidate manifest; never target a mutable checkout or shared development origin.",
    "Execution requires QA-owned isolated database, storage and server, real-device ingestion disconnected, and local verification that every frame is camera-free or generated synthetic-only before any screenshot may enter model/image tools.",
    "Fixture owner must release stable paused EQ-PROFILE-ROUTES at its 1000ms event and paused FG-FIRE at its 1000ms event, scenario position input, one active matching incident per mode, equipment workers A/B/C and fire-gas A/B, known B position. Equipment A/B/C and fire-gas A original/current incident records must exist; fire-gas B guidance is not assumed. Both mode fixtures retain preset sk1265-at6; no equipment mutations occur during this suite.",
    "Admin actorId and role are both admin. Access code comes only from QA_DEMO_ACCESS_CODE; this contract contains no fallback.",
    "The harness only posts session login; no scenario, profile, incident, calibration or equipment mutation is performed by this main surface matrix.",
    "Current records are captured as observed, including real expiry. No state here proves fresh current route validity. The C no-route case checks recorded policy output, not a still-valid live guidance window.",
    "Six-crane selection/motion, both-mode valid/no-route timing, route geometry, authenticated worker flows, broad failure fixtures, concurrent admins, playback, physical sources and performance remain independent runtime followups in surface-matrix-v1.md.",
    "The runner reports producer-browser-check and productAcceptance NOT_RUN; independently authored W3A execution/review provenance must be recorded separately, never rewrite its labels to PASS.",
    "31 logical states at five viewports = 155 semantic cases before overlapping focus frames; actual PNG count is determined at runtime."
  ],
